  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="358cab4b-040d-5163-b67b-d163439e0e12" activityNameId="e62339ca-e7d8-5db8-beb4-2cc45df19d6a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Silicon carbide, recycling, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Silicon carbide, recycling, at plant
The simple inventory for the production process is based on the raw material inputs. It recycles used sawing slurry from the wafer cutting process, to recover SiC and PEG (poly ethylene glycol). This re-cycling is usually done off-site by the slurry supplier and therefore modelled separately. Silicon is generally not recycled. Allocation among the products is based on the weight of all outputs.;
CAS number: 000409-21-2; 
Formula: SiC; 
Synonyms: silicon monocarbide, carborundum, carbolon; 
UUID: b2ddf8f6-8fd5-370a-a1a0-aec3aef77a26
Gate to gate inventory for recycling of slurry produced during wire sawing of silicon (Spec. Weight of input 1.75kg/l). Includes transport to recycling facility, electricity use and waste treatment.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technology.
Time period: Time of publication and data investigation.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature and internet. Average data from 3 companies. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b2ddf8f6-8fd5-370a-a1a0-aec3aef77a26.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
